-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 55.3(2)(c) and 60(9)(c) -- THE WINDOW AFTER INCAPACITY HAS CEASED (shared).
--
-- Sections 55.3 and 60 each let the Minister treat an application as made earlier because the applicant was
-- incapable of making it. Subsection 55.3(2) (division of unadjusted pensionable earnings) and subsection 60(9)
-- (benefits) have a paragraph (c) in the same words: the application must have been made "within the period that
-- begins on the day on which the person had ceased to be so incapable and that comprises the same number of days,
-- not exceeding twelve months, as in the period of incapacity", or, where that period comprises fewer than thirty
-- days, "not more than one month after the month in which the person had ceased to be so incapable". One rule
-- carries both, with both citations, so that the two cannot drift apart.

§ `The window after incapacity has ceased`

-- src:1610 | (c) the application was actually made or the information was actually received by the Minister
-- src:1611 | (i) within the period that begins on the day on which the person had ceased to be so incapable and that comprises the same number of days, not exceeding twelve months, as in the period of incapacity, or
-- src:1612 | (ii) where the period referred to in subparagraph (i) comprises fewer than thirty days, not more than one month after the month in which the person had ceased to be so incapable,
@ref Act s 55.3(2)(c) (src:1610-1612)
-- src:2054 | (c) the application was made
-- src:2055 | (i) within the period that begins on the day on which that person had ceased to be so incapable and that comprises the same number of days, not exceeding twelve months, as in the period of incapacity, or
-- src:2056 | (ii) where the period referred to in subparagraph (i) comprises fewer than thirty days, not more than one month after the month in which that person had ceased to be so incapable,
@ref Act s 60(9)(c) (src:2054-2056)
GIVEN `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` IS A DATE
      `the number of days in the period of incapacity` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`cp4 the application was made within the period after incapacity ceased` `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` `the number of days in the period of incapacity` `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received` MEANS
        `paragraph (c)(i) is met` OR `paragraph (c)(ii) is met`
    WHERE
        -- (c)(i): the period beginning on the day the person ceased to be incapable, with as many days as the
        -- period of incapacity but not more than twelve months. A period of n days beginning on a day ends on
        -- that day plus n - 1; a period of twelve months beginning on a day ends the day before its anniversary
        -- (NOTES.md, fork register).
        `the last day of the period in subparagraph (i)` MEANS
            IF (`the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` PLUS (`the number of days in the period of incapacity` MINUS 1)) AT MOST ((`add months` `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` 12) PLUS (0 MINUS 1))
            THEN `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` PLUS (`the number of days in the period of incapacity` MINUS 1)
            ELSE (`add months` `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` 12) PLUS (0 MINUS 1)
        `paragraph (c)(i) is met` MEANS
                `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received` AT LEAST `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable`
            AND `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received` AT MOST `the last day of the period in subparagraph (i)`
        -- (c)(ii): where the period in (i) comprises fewer than thirty days, not more than one month after the
        -- month in which the person ceased to be so incapable.
        `paragraph (c)(ii) is met` MEANS
                `the number of days in the period of incapacity` LESS THAN 30
            AND `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received` AT LEAST `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable`
            AND (`the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received`) AT MOST 1
